            <ArticleTitle>Changes and significance of serum angiopoietin-2 levels in patients with coronary heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>745-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/1354750X.2012.727028</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary heart disease (CHD) is characterized by inflammatory process and endothelial dysfunction. To investigate angiopoietin-2 (Ang-2) profiles, we evaluated serum Ang-2 levels in different types of CHD in 166 subjects. Ang-2 was measured by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay. Serum Ang-2 levels were significantly elevated in patients with CHD and gradually increased with advance of CHD. Ang-2 was positively correlated with Gensini scores and hs-CRP. Ang-2 might have potential implication in detecting and monitoring the progression of CHD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
